        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zimmerman%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Lake Fremont, a spring‑fed lake on Zimmerman’s eastern boundary, was named in 1856 after explorer John C. Frémont.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/zimmerman_minnesota",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Originally incorporated as the Village of Lake Fremont on January 29, 1910, the community became the City of Zimmerman in 1967.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/zimmerman_minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Zimmerman serves as the gateway to the Sherburne National Wildlife Refuge, one of the few remaining natural oak savannas in the United States.",
